<title>CHINA: HANG SENG UP ON CHINA STAKE SPECULATION.</title>
<headline>HANG SENG UP ON CHINA STAKE SPECULATION.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Hang Seng Bank Ltd soared on Monday as speculation resurfaced that a Chinese party may be interested in buying a stake in the bank, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;Renewed speculation that a Chinese firm might take a stake in the company ignited investors interest in the stock again,&quot; said a sales manager at a regional brokerage.</p>
<p>The shares rose HK$6.00, or 5.83 percent, to a session high of HK$109.00 in late trade on volume of 4.14 million shares.</p>
<p>Brokers said while the upside may be limited in the short term, the speculation could give the stock a boost in the longer run.</p>
<p>Hang Seng Bank officials declined to comment on the market talk.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong News Room (852) 2843 6370</p>
